---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { BUSINESS } from '../consts';

const stats = [
  { big: '25+', lbl: 'years deploying & managing technology' },
  { big: '80+', lbl: 'combined years behind the board' },
  { big: '$250', lbl: 'is where most monthly plans start' },
  { big: 'M2M', lbl: 'month-to-month — no lock-in, ever' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="AITS was built differently — on 25+ years of onboarding, integrating, deploying, and managing technology that has to keep working. One flat fee. Fixes included."
  path="/about"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-label">About AITS</span>
      <h1 class="section-heading">We do things differently.<br /><em>From the ground up.</em></h1>
      <p class="section-sub">
        AITS — Advanced Intelligent Technology Solutions — helps small and mid-sized businesses put
        AI to work so they compete with companies five times their size.
      </p>

      <div class="stat-strip">
        {
          stats.map((s) => (
            <div class="stat card">
              <div class="stat-big">{s.big}</div>
              <div class="stat-lbl">{s.lbl}</div>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <div class="story prose">
        <p>
          We were not built like most AI companies. We were built on 25+ years of onboarding,
          integrating, deploying, and managing software, hardware, and full solutions — through
          every era of business technology: the first office servers, the rise of the cloud, and
          everything in between. AI is our newest tool. It is not our first rodeo.
        </p>

        <h2>The week-three problem — <em>and why we exist.</em></h2>
        <p>
          Here is what we watched happen again and again: a business buys an AI solution, and it
          works beautifully on day one. Then week two or three arrives. One of the tools underneath
          pushes an update, a connection quietly breaks, and nobody on the team knows how to fix it.
          So they call the company that built it — and get billed. Every single time. That vendor's
          business model profits when things break.
        </p>
        <p>
          AITS is the inverse. One flat monthly fee covers the tools <em>and</em> the team that
          keeps them working — and we do not wait for your call. We run proactive maintenance: your
          website, your forms, your booking, your CRM, and every automation tested on a regular
          schedule. When something outside anyone's control changes — a platform like YouTube
          rewrites a rule overnight — we would rather find it before you do, and fix it right the
          first time so you are not calling twice about the same thing. Every "it's broken" call
          costs us, not you. That is what 25 years of managing technology teaches you: day one is
          easy. Month three is the difference.
        </p>

        <h2>An ecosystem, <em>not a toolbox.</em></h2>
        <p>
          The goal is bigger than a website or a handful of automations. We build your business an
          entire ecosystem — every visitor who hits your website or your social gets found,
          answered, followed up, booked, invoiced, and asked for a review, automatically. A site
          engineered with real search engine optimization <em>and</em> AI-search optimization, so
          customers discover you however they search. The result: for a very low cost, your company
          functions like a mid-sized organization or larger — with everything they have, at what
          would otherwise cost ten times as much.
        </p>

        <h2>A partnership that <em>grows with you.</em></h2>
        <p>
          This is a true business partnership, not a transaction. As your company grows, you will
          need more automation to keep your team focused on the work that drives revenue — not the
          busywork pulling them away from it. We grow with you: adding services, expanding
          automations, and finding the next hours to hand back to your people. Your growth is our
          roadmap — because we only grow when you grow.
        </p>

        <h2>We do not run pilots. <em>We deliver results.</em></h2>
        <p>
          Every engagement starts with an early win your entire team can see and feel. We start
          with the tasks your team hates most, automate those first, and make sure every person
          sees the benefit before we touch anything else. That is how adoption sticks — and
          adoption is where most AI deployments quietly fail.
        </p>

        <h2>Built by a next-generation founder. <em>Backed by decades of results.</em></h2>
        <p>
          {BUSINESS.founder} launched AITS with the vision and energy of a builder who grew up
          inside the technology industry. Behind him stands a board with over 80 combined years of
          managed services, AI deployment, and business leadership across North America — the same
          people whose operational discipline is built into how AITS runs every client's
          technology.
        </p>

        <h2>In your corner, <em>wherever you are.</em></h2>
        <p>
          AITS is headquartered in San Diego and serves businesses across the entire United States.
          In Southern California we can be on-site when something needs a human — everywhere else,
          you get the same team, the same platform, and the same response when something needs
          attention. And we work month-to-month: you stay because the results justify it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-cta">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary">Get your free AI assessment</a>
        <a href="/#different" class="btn-ghost">See how we're different</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .stat-strip {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 52px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 1080px) {
    .stat-strip {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .stat-strip {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
  .stat {
    padding: 22px 24px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .stat-big {
    font-family: var(--fran);
    font-size: 34px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--accent2);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }
  .stat-lbl {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-top: 6px;
  }
  .story h2 {
    font-family: var(--fran);
    font-size: clamp(20px, 2.6vw, 28px);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: 40px 0 12px;
  }
  .story h2 em {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--accent2);
  }
  .story p {
    color: var(--text2);
    font-size: 1.06rem;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
  .story p em {
    color: var(--teal2);
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .about-cta {
    display: flex;
    gap: 14px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 44px;
  }
</style>
